; link/pop_tiles.link — the BAKED TILE PAGE for one blueprint screen (P5.5).
;
; One 8,192 B GIME block at $C000, mapped through $FFA6 and pinned for the whole draw.
; `cel_pg_sig` is 0 in the gated design, so $FFA7 is never written and nothing rotates.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; $C000..$DFFF IS 8,192 B AND ALL OF IT IS REACHABLE — unlike $FFA7's page.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; link/pop_cels_pg.link records why the ROTATING page is 7,680 and not 8,192: gfx.s sets
; $FF90 with MC3=1, which holds $FE00-$FEFF as constant RAM, and $FF00-$FFFF is always
; I/O, so the top 512 B of whatever sits at $FFA7 cannot be reached through the window.
; NONE OF THAT APPLIES HERE. $FFA6's window ends at $DFFF, far below the constant page,
; so this script's budget really is the full block.
;
; harness/tools/bake_screen.py refuses to emit a page over 8,192 B, so the capacity check
; happens before the assembler sees anything — a build error rather than a silent overrun.
;
; The `load` value is bare hex. `section prog load $C000` parses the `$` form as ZERO —
; no error, no warning, exit 0, and the image lands at $0000. link/pop_cels_res.link
; documents that at length and decb_to_raw.py refuses an image whose first segment is not
; exactly at the `--base` build.bat states, which is what turns the silence into a failure.
;
; Comments here are `;`. lwlink does NOT accept `*` — that is an assembler convention and
; using it is a parse error, not a comment.

section prog load C000

entry tile_page
